messages.reasoning_content:
The `kubectl set` command failed because of how it interprets the complex command string with quotes and semicolons.

I must use a JSON patch for reliable modification of the container command.

I will patch the deployment `app` to change the command of the `app` container.
The container name is `app`.

New patch:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "command": ["sh", "-c", "while true; do echo alive > /tmp/heartbeat; sleep 5; done"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
This uses the array form for the command, which is the Kubernetes standard for executable definition.

I will execute the patch.

